int | $(x-2)^{3}$ | $(y-1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(1,2)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(3,2)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(1,0)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(3,0)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065421/assets/7e42173ebe7cbf85a1bca0bb8cff1bc95841e309b7cc737f84435c2a45485aa7.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-326445/field-1" "q-326445/field-2" "q-326445/field-3" "q-326445/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326445"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
